findings.proposedRule:
The baseline-solver rail (u05 r2 notes; still unwritten). Add an ITM-02 advisory for a three-option choice item that meets any of these conditions:
(a) the key alone has the maximum content-token overlap with promptDe;
(b) the key is the only option whose first token differs from the others (Ja against Nein, or the reverse);
(c) the key is at least 1.5 × as long as every distractor and is the only option with a coordinator.
Failing fixtures: a1.1-u06 ls2-i04 (a, b) and ls2-i01 (c). Passing fixtures: the two replacements above. The test runs over all registered courses.

verdict:
Not exit-ready. Most of the unit's own work is done: 0 BLOCKER, 1 MAJOR, 7 MINOR.

What r2 asked for has landed in the unit:
- the ls3-mo prompt and the ls1-mo English twin (r2-F02);
- the new ls2-i01 and the ls1-i01 distractors (r2-F03);
- the LS2 timeline (r2-F04);
- the lp1/lp2 split (r2-F08);
- the unit fallback of r2-F07;
- all four polish items.
The validator is green, identical to r2 (0 blocker, 22 ratchet, and 1 advisory, the known „Sie können“ false positive), and check.mjs reports 0 errors. We solved all 94 items blind and every key is right. 93 candidate answers behave as intended in the real grader. The exam blocks match sd1.json exactly and are original.

The MAJOR is unchanged and still not the author's. The Lernziele box on the Start and Check screens (F01) comes from a registry, a compiler and rails that are identical to r2. The five u06 texts still carry ob-, dass- and wenn-clauses, a zu-infinitive, a Perfekt and „passender Anrede“. This is stop-the-line for the level.

Four new minors are small data edits, each validated in a scratch copy:
- Two LS2 listening items can be solved by option shape or stem overlap (F02). One of them comes from r2's own proposal.
- A reserve explanation states a false rule, „Vor einem Nomen steht kein, nicht nicht“, which the unit's own rc.kein contradicts (F03).
- A (der) cue stands before Schlüssel, whose plural „die Schlüssel“ LS1 teaches one screen earlier (F04).
- Two 14-word input sentences exceed the profile's 12. No rail measures this, because TXT-01 is unbuilt (F05).

Three owner-held minors are carried unchanged: the nicht/kein ErrorTag (F06), the rule cards and spine (F07), and the lexicon roles (F08). F08 grows this round. „Liebe …“ and „Viele Grüße“, the Anrede and Gruß that the S2 task and the can-do require, are receptive throughout a1.1 and close eight S2 models. „Frage“ and „Wort“, allocated to u12, pass the rails only through a verb homograph and the metalanguage allowlist. The class now meets §9.4's stop-the-line threshold.

